body.zh-TW:
想讓 Claude 深入推理又擔心 token（AI 處理與計費的文字單位）消耗過量，現在能透過 `maxEffortLevel` 設定為思考深度加上緊箍咒。⟦這宛如在跑車油門踏板下方加裝限速卡榫，無論開在哪條公路上都能限制最高轉速，駕駛依舊能輕踩慢行，自訂路線的定速指示也不會被車廠出廠預設忽略。⟧以前在 Bedrock、Vertex 與 Foundry 等不同雲端平台上，很難全面鎖定努力程度上限。現在無論在最外層或 `modelSettings` 針對個別模型指定，都能統一設限，且日常仍可自由選擇更低的努力等級：
```
{
  "maxEffortLevel": "medium",
  "modelSettings": {
    "claude-opus-4-7": {
      "maxEffortLevel": "low"
    }
  }
}
```
此外，自訂指令、技能或子代理在 YAML 前言中指定的 `effort:` 數值，先前在 Opus 4.7、Opus 4.8 與 Fable 5 等固定預設等級的模型上會失效，如今已修復並能正確生效。

body.en:
If you want Claude to reason deeply without burning through excessive tokens, you can now cap its thinking depth with the `maxEffortLevel` setting. ⟦This is like installing a speed limiter stop beneath a sports car's accelerator pedal: it caps maximum RPM on any highway while still letting the driver cruise gently, ensuring custom cruise-control instructions along the route are no longer overridden by factory defaults.⟧ Previously across cloud providers like Bedrock, Vertex, and Foundry, it was difficult to uniformly lock effort level caps. Now, whether configured at the top level or per model under `modelSettings`, limits apply consistently while still allowing you to pick a lower effort level during daily use:
```
{
  "maxEffortLevel": "medium",
  "modelSettings": {
    "claude-opus-4-7": {
      "maxEffortLevel": "low"
    }
  }
}
```
Additionally, `effort:` values specified in YAML frontmatter for custom commands, skills, or subagents previously failed on models with pinned default effort levels (such as Opus 4.7, Opus 4.8, and Fable 5); this has now been fixed to take effect properly.

body.zh-TW:
企業管理者能透過 `managedMcpServers` 設定，統一派發 HTTP 或 SSE 的 MCP（Model Context Protocol，讓 AI 連接外部工具的協定）伺服器，格式同 `.mcp.json` 並略過本機指令：

```
{
  "managedMcpServers": {
    "company-docs": {"url": "https://mcp.internal.example.com/sse", "type": "sse"}
  }
}
```

`allowedMcpServers` 改為僅管制使用者新增的伺服器；升級後若要封鎖 `managed-mcp.json` 伺服器，需改用 `deniedMcpServers`。若管理設定檔、drop-in 檔案、MDM plist 或 HKLM 值解析失敗，Claude Code 會拒絕啟動並指名來源。由 MDM 或管理設定檔設定的 policy helper 執行後，`forceRemoteSettingsRefresh` 強制重整也修復生效。⟦這好比總務處配發公用設備，清單破損缺頁警衛就在大門攔下核對，絕不含糊放行。⟧

body.en:
Administrators can now distribute HTTP or SSE MCP servers (Model Context Protocol, which connects AI to external tools) to every user via the `managedMcpServers` setting, using the same format as `.mcp.json` while skipping local commands:

```
{
  "managedMcpServers": {
    "company-docs": {"url": "https://mcp.internal.example.com/sse", "type": "sse"}
  }
}
```

`allowedMcpServers` now governs only user-added servers; to block `managed-mcp.json` servers after upgrading, use `deniedMcpServers` instead. If the managed settings file, a drop-in file, the MDM plist, or the HKLM value fails to parse, Claude Code now refuses to start and names the source. Additionally, `forceRemoteSettingsRefresh` now properly triggers at startup even after a policy helper configured by MDM or managed settings has already run. ⟦It is like a company issuing standard equipment: if the manifest is torn or unreadable, the guard stops everyone at the gate to verify rather than letting unchecked gear through.⟧
